'''Libertad''' ({{IPA|bl|libeɾˈtad|link=yes}}; {{Literal translation|liberty}}; {{Langx|pt|Liberdade}}) is an [[Communes of Balisca|autonomous commune]] on the island of [[Pindorama]], an [[Indigenous nations in Balisca|Indigenous nation]] and [[communities of Balisca|community]] within [[Balisca]]. It is the xth-most populous city [[Catanduva]], the Xth in Pindorama, and is one of the fastest-growing cities in Balisca, mostly as a result of immigration from [[W:South America|South America]] (especially [[Brazil]] and [[W:Venezuela|Venezuela]]).  

The settlement was founded as a [[W:Quilombo|quilombo/palenque]] by formerly enslaved Africans that had escaped from Brazil via the [[Araucarian Passage]], and it later grew into the largest settlement of free and freed [[W:Afro-Caribbean|Afro-Caribbean]] and Liberated African slaves outside of the [[Maroon Confederacy]]. Their descendants are known as the [[Pindorama Creole people|Pindoramense Creoles]].

It is the westernmost city on the island of Pindorama, located on the [[La Libertad Peninsula]].

